# Expectation record for 08_gcc_extensions/001_statement_expressions.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_statement_expressions
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = Statement expressions in value position, including inside macros
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
Every statement expression yields an initialized value of a defined type, and each declares
its own local objects and assigns them before use, so no indeterminate value is read.  Any
macro argument that a statement expression could evaluate more than once is a simple
object or literal with no side effect, so no object is modified twice between sequence
points.  All arithmetic stays inside the range of int.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
The warning gate drops -pedantic for this program.  The subject under test is a GCC
extension, which is by definition not standard C, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
such constructs: with it in force the program could not be compiled at all and the feature
would go untested, which constraint C3 forbids.  Every other member of the gate is
retained, including -Werror, so no other class of defect in this program is downgraded.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
se_folded_max=12
se_folded_square=81
se_folded_triangle=55
se_folded_nested=10
se_folded_direct=6
se_folded_seq=7
se_folded_arg=5
se_runtime_max=12
se_runtime_square=81
se_runtime_triangle=55
se_runtime_nested=10
se_runtime_direct=6
se_runtime_seq=7
se_runtime_arg=8
END
